WEBVTT

00:36.000 --> 00:38.878
I am so bored.

00:39.045 --> 00:41.798
Hey, dog, when you take a break
from re-applying your lipstick,

00:41.881 --> 00:44.425
- how about taking me to the park?
- My lipstick? What?

00:46.010 --> 00:49.681
Oh, right, right.
Right, because of my penis.

00:49.807 --> 00:52.601
Yeah, that's fantastic.

00:52.810 --> 00:55.478
Lois, Brian won't take me to the park.

00:55.562 --> 00:58.064
Then he talked about his ding-dong.

00:58.148 --> 01:00.692
Lois. Lois!

01:00.775 --> 01:02.945
Damn it, woman! Pay attention to me!

01:03.195 --> 01:05.113
Stewie, that's not nice.

01:05.239 --> 01:08.408
Don't grab Mommy's pants like that.
You could really hurt her.

01:08.534 --> 01:12.538
Yes. Yes, I could, couldn't I?
I could hurt Mommy.

01:12.621 --> 01:15.374
Shame on us, Rupert.
How dare we succumb to boredom

01:15.499 --> 01:17.751
while that wretched woman
continues to breathe?

01:17.876 --> 01:20.754
She must be destroyed.
With Lois out of the way,

01:20.838 --> 01:24.467
I could finally focus on my life's ambition
of taking pictures of Madison County.

01:27.135 --> 01:28.889
Let's go back and take a bath.

01:29.014 --> 01:30.931
Yeah. How about you go back
and take a bath?

01:35.353 --> 01:37.564
Griffin, have you filed
those shipping reports yet?

01:37.647 --> 01:39.441
Angela, Angela, come here. Check this out.

01:39.566 --> 01:42.027
Look at what this chick is doing
to this polar bear.

01:42.111 --> 01:43.862
Wait, wait...

01:44.404 --> 01:47.282
Wait, wait, wait. It's coming up.

01:50.577 --> 01:51.953
There you are, Opie.

01:52.037 --> 01:55.082
Congratulations.
You made Employee of the Month again.

01:57.501 --> 01:59.462
How come I'm never
Employee of the Month?

01:59.588 --> 02:01.254
Man, this is the worst job I've had

02:01.338 --> 02:03.840
since I was the conductor
for the Sand People choir.

02:03.966 --> 02:05.426
And a one and a two.

02:09.597 --> 02:12.392
No, no, no, no! The altos were early.

02:12.475 --> 02:14.477
This is the worst glee club I've ever...

02:14.603 --> 02:16.187
Come on. Where are you going?

02:16.312 --> 02:18.356
- The benefit's tomorrow!
- Relax.

02:18.481 --> 02:20.900
The Sand People frighten easily
but they'll be back.

02:20.984 --> 02:22.151
And in greater numbers.

02:22.277 --> 02:23.778
Well, that'll give us a richer harmony.

02:23.903 --> 02:25.656
Oh, yeah. No, it's gonna sound fantastic.

02:38.461 --> 02:40.712
Help! Somebody! I'm blacking out.

02:42.506 --> 02:43.758
Brian, help me.

02:56.854 --> 02:59.481
That jerk, Opie,
got Employee of the Month again.

02:59.607 --> 03:01.150
All because my boss hates me.

03:01.233 --> 03:04.319
Maybe you need to brown-nose her
a little bit, Peter.

03:04.445 --> 03:06.239
Really? I thought you said she was ugly.

03:06.363 --> 03:08.158
Oh, you mean kiss up to her.

03:08.242 --> 03:09.742
That's a great idea, Joe.

03:09.867 --> 03:13.872
And if that doesn't do it, you could
always just work hard and be polite.

03:13.998 --> 03:16.792
<i>That's how I won friends
when I worked for E!</i>

03:17.000 --> 03:21.046
<i>Seabiscuit! Seabiscuit!
Would you mind talking to E!?</i>

03:21.171 --> 03:23.716
I'm not Seabiscuit. I'm Penelope Cruz.

03:23.840 --> 03:27.428
And you're just lovely.
Would you like a carrot?

03:30.806 --> 03:32.058
Good girl.

03:32.350 --> 03:36.061
Brown-nose, huh?
All right. I'll do something special for her.

03:41.526 --> 03:42.609
Surprise!

03:42.735 --> 03:45.029
Griffin, what the hell
are you doing at my house?

03:45.113 --> 03:47.907
Well, I asked around the office
and everybody said you liked animals,

03:48.033 --> 03:50.202
so I organized a surprise cockfight.

03:52.954 --> 03:56.541
Oh, boy. Oh, boy. Oh, God.

03:57.667 --> 04:00.379
Well, looks like they killed each other.

04:01.589 --> 04:04.843
That's probably what all that racket was
about an hour ago.

04:05.800 --> 04:08.304
Well, I will see you Monday.

04:17.688 --> 04:19.022
Oh, crap.

04:20.066 --> 04:24.237
Well, looks like the good Lord
just sent me a conversation starter.

04:24.320 --> 04:26.906
Come here, Jesse. Come get the ball.

04:49.011 --> 04:50.639
How unfortunate.

04:50.765 --> 04:53.934
Miss Hobson, Stewie's really been
acting out a lot at home.

04:54.018 --> 04:57.271
And I was just wondering,
how's he been behaving at school?

04:57.813 --> 05:01.608
Mrs. Griffin, let me show you
some pictures he drew in class.

05:06.780 --> 05:09.658
- Notice anything unusual?
- I sure do.

05:09.742 --> 05:12.328
- His father's not in any of them.
- Exactly.

05:12.453 --> 05:15.831
Well, Peter's been very preoccupied
with work lately.

05:15.956 --> 05:20.087
I guess Stewie's been missing his father.
Thank you for letting me know.

05:21.837 --> 05:23.131
Damn! She moved.

05:23.256 --> 05:26.468
Well, I suppose it's not the first time
someone's made a miscalculation.

05:31.139 --> 05:32.807
What happens to us in the future, Doc?

05:32.933 --> 05:35.727
It's your kids, Marty. Something's
gotta be done about your kids.

05:35.852 --> 05:38.188
- What do you mean?
- Your daughter marries a black man.

05:39.356 --> 05:42.443
- That's actually not a big deal for me.
- Yeah, me neither.

05:43.360 --> 05:46.237
Well, it... Well, it... You... Really?

05:46.363 --> 05:48.490
Yeah. I mean, what's wrong with that?

05:48.616 --> 05:52.579
No, no, nothing, nothing.
It's nothing, I guess. I think it's great.

05:52.704 --> 05:54.163
Congratulations.

05:54.371 --> 05:56.291
I don't think I'm comfortable
around you anymore.

05:56.375 --> 05:58.710
Did you know peanut butter
was invented by a black man?

05:58.835 --> 05:59.794
Too late, Doc.

06:05.049 --> 06:07.218
Hi, Herbert. What brings you here?

06:07.343 --> 06:11.222
It seems your son's baseball
broke one of my windows the other day.

06:11.348 --> 06:13.891
Oh, my God. I am so sorry.

06:14.017 --> 06:16.688
Chris, this is gonna come out
of your allowance.

06:17.395 --> 06:19.482
Perhaps we could work something out.

06:19.566 --> 06:23.694
I could use a strapping young man
to do some chores around my house.

06:23.776 --> 06:25.070
That seems fair to me.

06:25.195 --> 06:27.363
Chris, you have damaged
this man's property.

06:27.489 --> 06:30.784
And until you pay off the debt,
you'll do whatever job he wants you to do.

06:30.909 --> 06:32.703
And at the end of the day,
if you're exhausted

06:32.787 --> 06:35.956
and your face is dripping wet, well,
that just means you did a good job.

06:36.082 --> 06:37.667
That sounds fine.

06:37.958 --> 06:40.836
I don't want to spend my weekend
doing chores.

06:40.920 --> 06:43.213
You know, Chris,
a little hard work can do wonders.

06:43.339 --> 06:45.257
Just look at how they built the pyramids.

06:45.383 --> 06:48.261
They say all peoples
must go through some hard times.

06:48.344 --> 06:50.763
Well, we Jews are getting ours
out of the way early.

06:50.847 --> 06:54.266
From here on out,
it's gonna be nothing but smooth sailing.

06:56.769 --> 06:58.188
I have an announcement to make.

06:58.270 --> 07:01.274
Don't you do it.
Don't you lose a single pound.

07:01.400 --> 07:03.735
I don't care what
those Hollywood image-makers say.

07:03.818 --> 07:04.903
Big women are sexy.

07:05.029 --> 07:06.029
I wanted to tell you

07:06.113 --> 07:09.116
that Opie will not be receiving
Employee of the Month,

07:09.200 --> 07:10.743
because he's being promoted.

07:10.867 --> 07:13.203
Oh, yes!
That means I'm Employee of the Month.

07:13.286 --> 07:16.541
No, you're not, Griffin.
I'm giving it to Soundwave.

07:16.623 --> 07:19.126
<i>So, I can just put my stuff anywhere?</i>

07:22.380 --> 07:25.425
<i>My wife, Denise.
We met in a Christian chat room.</i>

07:28.093 --> 07:32.265
- Peter, we need to talk about your son.
- The fat one or the funny-looking one?

07:33.182 --> 07:34.934
Dad called you fat.

07:35.268 --> 07:36.310
Wait.

07:36.435 --> 07:38.105
Stewie's really been acting out lately.

07:38.188 --> 07:40.774
And, I think it's 'cause
he's not spending enough time with you.

07:40.899 --> 07:43.108
It's time that you take an interest
in your son.

07:43.192 --> 07:46.404
Starting today, I want you to spend
more time with Stewie.

07:46.780 --> 07:47.865
Okay.

07:47.989 --> 07:49.574
You can make a box fort.

07:49.658 --> 07:52.077
See? Here's a box.
You can pretend it's a fort.

07:52.160 --> 07:54.454
Actually, that sounds like fun. I want this.

07:54.538 --> 07:56.456
I'm king in here.

07:56.623 --> 07:59.709
Peter, maybe Stewie
would like to play fort, too.

07:59.835 --> 08:02.922
No! If you need me, I'll be in space.

08:07.426 --> 08:09.594
Great idea bringing Stewie
to Fenway Park, Peter.

08:09.678 --> 08:11.973
Yeah. There's no better place
for a father and son

08:12.056 --> 08:14.392
to really get to know each other
than a ballgame.

08:14.517 --> 08:15.643
Where is Stewie?

08:19.104 --> 08:20.648
Is that a baby in there?

08:20.732 --> 08:23.317
Oh, my God! He's gonna miss the game.

08:25.529 --> 08:27.864
Hey, you guys.
You remember those hot homeless twins

08:27.989 --> 08:30.033
who live under the overpass?
Well, last night I...

08:30.158 --> 08:32.619
Wait, wait, Quagmire.
Let me cover Stewie's ears.

08:46.676 --> 08:49.428
And this is the hand
that caused all the trouble.

08:49.803 --> 08:51.514
Got your nose, little guy.

08:56.185 --> 09:00.439
Peter, did you take Stewie to a strip club?
He smells like sweat and fear.

09:00.565 --> 09:04.320
Let me tell you, Tuesday afternoon
is not exactly their A squad.

09:04.402 --> 09:06.111
I actually saw bullet wounds.

09:06.237 --> 09:09.407
You can't just take him places
you want to go. He's a baby.

09:09.532 --> 09:12.827
Look, Lois, I think I know how
to spend time with my own kid, all right?

09:12.910 --> 09:15.162
The bond between a father and son
is sacred.

09:17.415 --> 09:20.211
I'm sorry, Jesus. But my house, my rules.

09:20.335 --> 09:23.005
Up yours, Joseph. You're not my real dad.

09:26.175 --> 09:28.385
- Hello?
- Hey, Dad, it's me.

09:28.552 --> 09:31.347
Listen, things here
aren't working out anymore.

09:31.431 --> 09:32.723
And I was just... I was wondering,

09:32.807 --> 09:35.268
can I come live with you and Janet
for a while?

09:35.392 --> 09:38.063
Wow, kiddo. You know, I'd love that,

09:38.145 --> 09:41.523
but I don't know if now is the best time.
Maybe next year, okay?

09:41.607 --> 09:44.694
I'll see you Friday night.
Tell your mother I sent the check.

09:44.776 --> 09:47.739
- So, where were we?
- Right about here.

09:48.698 --> 09:52.327
- Come on, baby, it's my birthday.
- No.

09:52.452 --> 09:55.245
All I'm saying is that
you just need to find an activity

09:55.330 --> 09:57.499
that you and Stewie can share.

09:57.624 --> 10:00.210
Peter, can you reach that box of rice?

10:00.752 --> 10:02.295
Oh, sorry, Lois.

10:03.964 --> 10:05.798
That rice got you, bitch.

10:06.967 --> 10:08.259
Hey, Stewie's laughing.

10:08.385 --> 10:10.304
Hey, you think that's funny?
Hey, you like that?

10:10.429 --> 10:13.015
Hey, Lois, you want some beans
with that rice?

10:14.391 --> 10:16.101
I misjudged you, fat man.

10:16.184 --> 10:17.894
Damn it. Peter, what's wrong with you?

10:17.978 --> 10:20.481
Wait, Lois, Lois, don't move.
Stewie's loving this.

10:22.317 --> 10:24.069
See if she's got any cash on her.

10:27.988 --> 10:30.116
Okay, Stewie, get the camera ready.

10:33.160 --> 10:34.454
Peter, stop it!

10:34.537 --> 10:36.455
What the hell are you doing?

10:36.539 --> 10:38.916
What do you think I'm doing?
I'm bonding with Stewie.

10:47.009 --> 10:50.138
There is nothing more precious
than a baby's laughter.

11:39.187 --> 11:41.856
- Jeez, I hope she can get out.
- I'm sure she'll be fine.

11:44.443 --> 11:46.111
Well, hello there, young man.

11:46.237 --> 11:48.572
I was starting to think
you weren't coming.

11:48.697 --> 11:50.699
Sorry I'm late, Mr. Herbert.

11:50.782 --> 11:52.619
Well, I guess I'll get started.

11:52.744 --> 11:55.580
You know, if you get sweaty
and want to take your shirt off,

11:55.705 --> 11:57.164
that'd be just fine.

11:57.288 --> 11:59.584
Or tie it in a knot, your choice.

12:03.671 --> 12:07.174
<i>We now go live to Ollie Williams
in the Channel Five traffic copter.</i>

12:07.258 --> 12:09.260
<i>- What's the scene, Ollie?
- Everybody looks like ants!</i>

12:09.386 --> 12:10.637
<i>Probably because you're up so high.</i>

12:10.761 --> 12:14.057
<i>Coming up next,
an exclusive interview with Andrew Shue.</i>

12:14.182 --> 12:16.601
Hey, hey, Dad, Dad, pull my finger.

12:17.268 --> 12:21.231
Wait... Sounded like a peep toad.
But it's not summer.

12:23.733 --> 12:26.694
Hey, drippy. You're back.
What's for dinner?

12:26.778 --> 12:30.782
Peter, when I said bond with Stewie,
this is not what I had in mind.

12:30.949 --> 12:34.411
- I am furious with you!
- You can't talk to him like that.

12:35.788 --> 12:37.080
Take that!

12:37.832 --> 12:41.377
- Stewie, you're going to your room.
- I think not, Dad's got my back.

12:41.461 --> 12:43.963
Stewie, she looks mad.
You better go to your room.

12:44.047 --> 12:47.466
What's the matter with you, fat man?
Stop her. Help me, you fool.

12:47.592 --> 12:50.761
You traitor.
I trusted you but you're a wuss!

12:50.845 --> 12:52.556
Don't feel bad, Peter.

12:52.638 --> 12:54.390
Hey, I know what'll cheer you up.

12:54.474 --> 12:57.393
- No, I don't think I'm in the mood.
- Are you sure?

13:15.495 --> 13:18.124
Sorry, Brian. It's just not doing it today.

13:32.554 --> 13:35.142
Hey, Stewie.
You got a minute for your daddy?

13:35.225 --> 13:37.101
Get out of here, you spineless oaf!

13:37.184 --> 13:40.188
Oh, and by the way,
I faked all those bowel movements.

13:40.522 --> 13:41.815
Brian, I feel awful.

13:41.940 --> 13:44.859
Stewie and I were getting along so good
and now he hates me.

13:44.985 --> 13:47.320
- How do I get him to like me again?
- Well, that depends.

13:47.404 --> 13:50.615
Do you really want my advice or are
you just asking random questions again?

13:50.699 --> 13:51.909
What's a hypotenuse?

13:54.077 --> 13:56.038
Stewie, I know you're a little mad at me
right now.

13:56.162 --> 13:59.124
But, when you see where I'm taking you,
you're gonna change your mind.

13:59.208 --> 14:01.294
Yeah, right. I'm gonna change my mind.

14:01.377 --> 14:05.756
We just sat on a plane for three hours
to come to Florida, God's waiting room,

14:05.880 --> 14:07.090
for who knows what...

14:09.301 --> 14:11.637
Disney World! Disney World!
Disney World!

14:11.721 --> 14:14.849
I want to go to Disney World!
Disney World! Disney World!

14:16.475 --> 14:17.978
I'm still mad at you.

14:25.568 --> 14:28.279
Hey, check it out, Stewie.
Halle Berry's Wild Ride.

14:39.916 --> 14:43.128
Wow! It looks like
Michael Jackson's coming right at me.

14:45.421 --> 14:49.302
I say, we've been puttering around
this fat farm for hours. I've had enough.

14:49.719 --> 14:51.720
Hey, Stewie, they got... Stewie?

14:52.222 --> 14:55.725
Oh, my God, he's gone.
Has anyone seen my son? Hello?

14:55.850 --> 14:57.685
<i>Hey, it's the crows from Dumbo.</i>

14:57.768 --> 14:59.103
Hey, you guys seen my son?

14:59.228 --> 15:04.024
Well, I done seen about everything but
I sure enough ain't seen your boy, no how!

15:04.318 --> 15:06.861
That's good old-fashioned family racism.

15:13.660 --> 15:18.248
Well, well, a lost child.
Looks like we've got a new recruit.

15:20.918 --> 15:23.169
- Now sing.
- I shall do no such thing.

15:23.295 --> 15:24.378
You must sing.

15:24.461 --> 15:28.466
If you don't, they'll make you do
a Christmas movie with Tim Allen.

15:36.517 --> 15:39.311
Is Chris still doing chores
for that disgusting old man?

15:39.436 --> 15:41.104
Meg, that's not nice.

15:41.188 --> 15:44.816
Old people have a lot to offer society.
Just look at Kim Catrall.

15:45.901 --> 15:47.903
Come and get it, big boy.

15:49.447 --> 15:50.532
Oh, damn.

15:54.159 --> 15:55.954
There we go.

16:02.002 --> 16:04.086
Thanks for buying me dinner, Mr. Herbert.

16:04.171 --> 16:07.299
I wanted to thank you properly
for all your hard work.

16:07.424 --> 16:09.967
- Souvenir photograph?
- Hell, yes.

18:22.230 --> 18:23.565
Are you dead?

18:39.164 --> 18:41.209
I say, fat man. Get me out of here.

18:41.333 --> 18:44.921
Stewie, there you are. Thank God.
Why are you dressed like Rerun?

18:48.091 --> 18:51.968
You're free, children. Run back
to your individual countries of origin.

18:52.052 --> 18:53.137
Hey!

18:53.304 --> 18:56.515
Those multi-cultural slave children
belong to the Disney Corporation.

18:56.641 --> 18:57.975
Get them, Achmed.

19:00.478 --> 19:02.938
Hey, look over there.
There's a woman learning.

19:12.239 --> 19:13.450
Quick, in here.

19:50.071 --> 19:51.947
Looks like we're in the clear.

19:52.490 --> 19:54.742
- Michael Eisner.
- Cover your heart.

19:54.867 --> 19:57.162
Kali Ma!

19:57.329 --> 19:59.331
Kali Ma!

19:59.455 --> 20:02.084
Kali Ma!

20:02.209 --> 20:04.087
You betrayed the shareholders.

20:14.014 --> 20:15.055
You think he's dead?

20:15.180 --> 20:17.100
No, no. He'll be back on his feet in no time,

20:17.225 --> 20:19.102
probably follow
in Jonathan Dolgen's footsteps,

20:19.227 --> 20:21.061
wind up with a pod deal
over at Touchstone.

20:21.144 --> 20:22.688
You all right, Stewie?

20:22.772 --> 20:24.065
You know what, fat man?

20:24.149 --> 20:26.651
I'm not sure how to say this
without sounding cheesy,

20:26.776 --> 20:30.071
but, well, you really came through
for me today. So I...

20:31.614 --> 20:32.907
What the hell.

20:33.366 --> 20:37.912
I love you, too, buddy.
Come on, Stewie. Let's go home.

20:38.663 --> 20:41.958
Florida. Just think,
somewhere in this state right now,

20:42.292 --> 20:44.878
Jeb Bush is eating a live puppy.

20:47.005 --> 20:51.468
Well, Jesse, I guess we got to find
some other way to spend our evenings.

20:51.968 --> 20:54.596
<i>And now back
to ESPN's exclusive coverage</i>

20:54.721 --> 20:56.432
<i>of the Little League World Series.</i>

20:56.557 --> 20:58.267
Oh, jackpot!

20:58.268 --> 21:59.268
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru